D17 — Environment-issue reporting: DONE

Summary
-------
Adds the `report_environment_issue({message, details})` tool so an agent records a
local-environment failure instead of trying to fix the environment, and returns
guidance to continue (rely on CI / skip the local step). Implemented end to end:

  - Tool + registry:      src/tools/environmentIssueTools.ts, src/index.ts, src/server/runTools.ts
  - Agent event:          src/agent/events.ts
  - Prompt rule (gated):  src/agent/prompt.ts (rule added only when the tool is enabled)
  - Protocol mapping:     src/protocol/{events,types,socket}.ts, packages/shared/src/socket.ts
  - Web UI card:          packages/web/src/components/chat/EnvironmentIssueCard.tsx + EventList.tsx
  - i18n (en + ar):       packages/web/src/i18n/{en,ar}.{json,ts}

Acceptance criteria (AC) met
----------------------------
  - tool records the issue + emits an event .......... src/tools/__tests__/environmentIssueTools.test.ts,
                                                       src/protocol/__tests__/environmentIssue.test.ts
  - prompt contains the rule (gated by tool availability) ... src/agent/__tests__/prompt.test.ts
  - UI card renders (web vitest) ..................... src/components/chat/__tests__/EnvironmentIssueCard.test.tsx
                                                       + new EventList integration test

Changes made in this session (continuing from commit 9c88a2c)
------------------------------------------------------------
  - Fixed an over-specified assertion in src/agent/__tests__/prompt.test.ts. The test
    conflated the always-on master-prompt tool *catalog* (§6.1, which names
    report_environment_issue unconditionally by design) with the conditional guidance
    *rule*. The assertion now gates the actual rule text (/rely on CI/i,
    /Do not report the step as passed/i, /When a step cannot run because of the local
    environment/i). Production code was NOT weakened.
  - Added packages/web/src/components/chat/__tests__/environmentIssueEventList.test.tsx
    proving the card renders through the live chat timeline (EventList -> ChatEventRow
    -> EnvironmentIssueCard), not just the component in isolation.

