Merge with manus-parity (97c53d7): resolved, all conflicts keep both sides
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
The merge gate (`git merge manus-parity`) conflicted in 7 files. Every conflict was
resolved by keeping BOTH sides; no test was weakened and no code was dropped:

  1. .jdone: add/add D17 marker vs the parity D4/N20 marker. Both preserved below.
  2. packages/shared/src/socket.ts: D17 `EnvironmentIssueEvent` + D4
     `PlanApprovalRequestedEvent`/`PlanApprovalResolvedEvent`, and the `ChatEvent`
     union extended with all three.
  3. packages/web/src/components/chat/EventList.tsx: import list now carries both
     `EnvironmentIssueEvent` (D17) and `CacheUsageEvent` (parity).
  4. src/agent/events.ts: `environment_issue` (D17) + `plan_approval_required` (D4)
     variants both kept.
  5. src/protocol/events.ts: both event imports and both switch cases kept.
     6. src/protocol/socket.ts: both `environment_issue` and `plan_approval_required`
     decode branches kept.
     7. src/protocol/types.ts: `EnvironmentIssueEvent` + the D4 plan-approval events
     both kept.

The merge also exposed one real defect, fixed (not worked around):
- `src/graph/runGraph.ts`: manus-parity made the `AgentEvent` switch exhaustive, so
  D17's `environment_issue` event hit the `default` arm and tsc failed with
  "Type '...environment_issue...' is not assignable to type 'never'". It is now
  mapped to a finished `note` node (the report is terminal: the agent records it and
  continues rather than asking the user), and a new case in
  `src/graph/__tests__/runGraph.test.ts` covers it. D17 shipped before the exhaustive
  switch existed on parity, so this was a merge-time interaction, not a pre-existing
  failure.

